    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40703" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rĕdargūtĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		redarguo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a refutation</i>, <i>reproof</i>, <i>defence</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">non habens in ore suo refutationes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Psa. 37, 15</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in redargutionem venire,</span>”
				<i>to fall into contempt</i>, <i>be mocked at</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Act. 19, 27</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Psa. 37, 15</span></i>; Boëth. Arist.
			Elench. 1 pr.</div>
